Lord Kṛṣṇa blew His conchshell, called Pāñcajanya;
Arjuna blew his, the Devadatta;
and Bhīma, the voracious eater and performer of herculean tasks, blew his terrific conchshell, called Pauṇḍra.

A transcendentalist should always engage his body, mind and self in relationship with the Supreme;
he should live alone in a secluded place and should always carefully control his mind.
He should be free from desires and feelings of possessiveness.

The Supreme Personality of Godhead said:
Son of Prith, a transcendentalist engaged in auspicious activities does not meet with destruction either in this world or in the spiritual world;
one who does good, My friend, is never overcome by evil.
